{
  "work_id": "scripture/armenian/job",
  "source_path": "scripture/armenian/job.json",
  "source_language": "hye",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12": {
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-10-12",
      "script": "scripts.embed_eval.translate"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.1.4",
      "source_sha256": "3aaa97506e3f0388",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "His sons would gather together and hold feasts with one another every day, taking their three sisters with them to eat and drink with them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.1.9",
      "source_sha256": "76f861da1148931f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Satan answered and said to the Lord, “Does Job worship the Lord for nothing?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.1.21",
      "source_sha256": "50c52bd6de02a67a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he said, “Naked I came from my mother’s womb, and naked I will return there.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.2.5",
      "source_sha256": "f17064ab1bc93df2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“Otherwise, please stretch out your hand and strike his bones and his flesh, and see whether he will not bless you to your face.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.2.10",
      "source_sha256": "4117faac5db525b6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He looked at her and said, “You have spoken like one of the foolish women. If we have received good things from the Lord’s hand, should we not endure these evils?” In all these things that happened to him, Job did not sin with his lips before the Lord, nor did he attribute folly to God."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.3.9",
      "source_sha256": "c43f7522ecbf2291",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Let the stars of that night grow dark; let it wait and not come into the light, and let it not see the morning star rising."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.4.14",
      "source_sha256": "4ebe74f6472a678f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Trembling and terror came upon me and shook my bones violently."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.5.9",
      "source_sha256": "0a8327d6467c684a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Who does great and unsearchable things, glorious things and wondrous works beyond number."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.5.21",
      "source_sha256": "edf78021aa820720",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He will hide you from the torments of the tongue, and you will not fear the evils coming upon you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.6.6",
      "source_sha256": "a27c9b95e4061606",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Can bread be eaten without salt, or is there any flavor in empty words?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.6.7",
      "source_sha256": "6b4c001119c9909b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "My soul cannot endure this, for I see my food with pus, like the smell of a lion."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.6.9",
      "source_sha256": "d30f39dee26ae2d9",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The Lord has begun to wound me, but let him not kill me altogether."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.6.10",
      "source_sha256": "87f21b6d243b0aa8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "May my city be my grave, upon whose walls I used to walk. I will not spare it, for I will not falsify the words of my holy God."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.6.13",
      "source_sha256": "14f451514209b150",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Now my help has been driven away from me, and mercy has withdrawn from me; the Lord’s care has passed me by."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.7.2",
      "source_sha256": "72fd17c7c538baea",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Or like a slave afraid of his master and hiding in the shade, or like a hired worker waiting for his wages."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.7.14",
      "source_sha256": "5e057d5dcef60893",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "You terrify me with dreams and strike me with visions."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.8.8",
      "source_sha256": "922ec5eef10e03dc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But please ask the earliest generation, and investigate according to the families of the fathers."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.9.3",
      "source_sha256": "13b59400ee5b0e51",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For if he wished to dispute with him, he would not listen to him, for he would not answer even one word out of a thousand."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.9.11",
      "source_sha256": "496c238fadb41f7d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If he passes over me, I will not see him; and if he passes beside me, even then I will not know it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.9.23",
      "source_sha256": "db1c32609255db7b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For the wicked will perish by a terrible death, but the righteous are mocked, for they are handed over into the hands of the ungodly."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.9.26",
      "source_sha256": "524bc8ff352a7dae",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Or is there any trace of the path of ships, or of an eagle flying in search of food?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.9.30",
      "source_sha256": "78a537c4fa1b9bd1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If I wash myself by hand and cleanse myself with clean hands."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.11.15",
      "source_sha256": "321100e04a01908e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then your face will shine like clear water; you will strip away filth and will not be afraid."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.12.7",
      "source_sha256": "3a10675c2e937187",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But please ask the four-footed animals whether they will tell you, and the birds of heaven whether they will explain it to you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.12.13",
      "source_sha256": "c2a28ee100b2b3ea",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Wisdom and strength come from him; counsel and understanding are his."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.12.14",
      "source_sha256": "a5e43fe2bbb5e2e9",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If he tears down, who will build? And if he shuts someone in, who will open?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.12.15",
      "source_sha256": "0818473fc959a279",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If he holds back the waters, he dries up the earth; and if he lets them loose, he destroys it, overturning it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.13.1",
      "source_sha256": "71791b607b5f91ad",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Look, my eye has seen all this, and my ear has heard it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.13.16",
      "source_sha256": "551ac1cda0a90ec3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And this will turn out to be my salvation, for deceit will not come before him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.13.17",
      "source_sha256": "da81188a1e711523",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Listen, listen to my words, for I will speak to you in your hearing."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.14.3",
      "source_sha256": "3e9f9aaf35d40d6f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Will you not indeed take account of him too? And you have made him enter into judgment before you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.14.12",
      "source_sha256": "5be0f4ae08bc1a5c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And a man lies down and will not rise. Until the heavens cease to exist, they will not be restored or wake from their sleep."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.15.10",
      "source_sha256": "a73c1e1aea574b9f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Indeed, among us there is one who is old and advanced in days, older than your father."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.15.20",
      "source_sha256": "d3e12f62ded20eec",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The whole life of the ungodly is full of anxieties; a fixed number of years is given to the mighty."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.15.25",
      "source_sha256": "1431a498799f3f44",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For he raised his hands against the Lord and rebelled before the Lord Almighty."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.17.10",
      "source_sha256": "99783cccf573a57d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But now, please, come and rise up, all of you, for I find no truth among you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.17.15",
      "source_sha256": "5615026a31bda47c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Now where is my hope? Or will I see my good fortune?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.18.2",
      "source_sha256": "fe638cb1ee02ce41",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "How long will you refuse to stop? Be quiet, so that we too may speak."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.19.9",
      "source_sha256": "e8e74a57468ae7ea",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He stripped me of my glory and removed the crown from my head."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.20.6",
      "source_sha256": "d19e4d12fa83a067",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Even if his offerings rise to heaven and his sacrifices approach the clouds."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.20.11",
      "source_sha256": "9a551bcbf560a734",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "His bones will be filled with his youth and will lie down with him in the dust."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.20.13",
      "source_sha256": "8a0d9f960463f84b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He will cherish it and not let it go, and will hold it within his throat."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.20.28",
      "source_sha256": "2252629bbce6ba20",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Destruction will utterly tear down his house; the day of wrath will come upon him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.22.18",
      "source_sha256": "d89696e3443d962a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And he filled their houses with good things, but the counsel of the ungodly is far from him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.23.13",
      "source_sha256": "06fa791c306e1882",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But if he has judged in this way, who could oppose him? For he did whatever he himself wished."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.24.3",
      "source_sha256": "d0f314bdceeebd3b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "They drove away the orphan’s donkey and took the widow’s ox as a pledge."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.24.7",
      "source_sha256": "27be57d23e194691",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "They made many lie down naked, without clothing; they stripped the clothes from their bodies."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.24.23",
      "source_sha256": "71b5d20400d6062c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Let him become sick and not expect to recover, but fall through disease, for his arrogance has tormented many."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.26.9",
      "source_sha256": "c6f5eebe4d3fed9d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He who holds the face of the throne spreads his cloud over it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.27.3",
      "source_sha256": "b746df319616792b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If my breath is still in me, and the spirit from God is around me, in my nostrils."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.29.6",
      "source_sha256": "d8b07e9def91ded6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When my paths were drenched with butter and my mountains were watered with milk."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.30.6",
      "source_sha256": "01853f8ebf1853ed",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Thieves rose against me, whose homes were holes in the rocks."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.30.16",
      "source_sha256": "5d6c9cf3de07f0c5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And now my soul will be poured out within me; days of pain have taken hold of me."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.30.18",
      "source_sha256": "a3ed2d7e2f668069",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "With great force he seized my robe and surrounded me like the band of my robe."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.30.22",
      "source_sha256": "f9101a2c350b8dcc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "You placed me in pain and cast me away from deliverance."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.31.4",
      "source_sha256": "619d7bb8551d08c5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Does he not himself see my ways, and will not all my steps be counted?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.31.19",
      "source_sha256": "4ff7168e20733743",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Did I disregard a naked person who was perishing and fail to clothe him?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.31.38",
      "source_sha256": "be80f2336abdd9b0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Has the earth ever groaned because of me, and have its furrows wept together?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.32.14",
      "source_sha256": "bc928913e2f104d8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And allow one man to speak such words."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.33.5",
      "source_sha256": "dabf7fe6f39a1e6e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "If you can, give me an answer to this; otherwise, be silent."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.33.19",
      "source_sha256": "e97ebf9b93010d5e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Again he rebuked him with sickness in bed and numbed his many bones."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.33.21",
      "source_sha256": "537b11bd08dd3111",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Until his flesh rots away and his bones are exposed bare."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.35.13",
      "source_sha256": "0bd3691c371b84b8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For the Lord does not wish to see disorder, for the Almighty himself sees those who commit lawlessness, and he will save me."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.35.14",
      "source_sha256": "439148ba56250f73",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Plead your case before him, if you can praise him as he is."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.35.16",
      "source_sha256": "821268c131133230",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So Job opens his mouth in vain and multiplies words in ignorance."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.36.26",
      "source_sha256": "bd06cd0767707cef",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Behold, the Mighty One is great, and we cannot know the number of his endless years."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.6",
      "source_sha256": "a47ad40f8e7f7633",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He commands the snow, saying, “Be on the earth,” and the winter rains according to their strength."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.9",
      "source_sha256": "d8a026a89bd7c0d7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Dew comes out of the storehouses, and cold from the heights."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.13",
      "source_sha256": "b885746255b59b3d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Whether for correction, or for his earth, or for mercy, they will find him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.14",
      "source_sha256": "48d23c1355415900",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Listen to this, Job; stand still and reflect on the Lord’s power."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.17",
      "source_sha256": "bab401b34241743f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And your warm robe rests quietly upon the earth."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.19",
      "source_sha256": "009c2cc27e7663d0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But why, indeed? Please teach me what we should say to him, and let us stop speaking at length."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.37.21",
      "source_sha256": "da259a0a1064a77a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Light is not visible to everyone; it shines in ancient times [?], like the light from him upon the clouds."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.40.1",
      "source_sha256": "8784daebc0e5b135",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Again the Lord speaks once more to Job from the cloud."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.40.17",
      "source_sha256": "483123658d21eb9f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Great trees shade him, together with the woods and the branches of the chaste tree."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.41.10",
      "source_sha256": "96bcb04dd6f2505e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 2,
      "text": "Blazing torches come from his mouth, and sparks of fire burst out and fall."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/armenian/job#Job.41.22",
      "source_sha256": "c9efee76c5425b33",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 2,
      "text": "He makes the depths boil like a pot; he regards the sea as nothing."
    }
  ]
}
